{
  "slug": "causal-discovery-and-structure-learning",
  "concept": "Causal Discovery and Structure Learning",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "Causal discovery (a.k.a. structure learning) learns the causal graph itself",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Causal discovery (a.k.a. structure learning) learns the causal graph itself",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "from observational and/or interventional data - the edges and their directions —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "rather than assuming the graph and estimating an effect. This is the upstream",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "problem to causal inference.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This skill (discovery): \"What is the causal structure? Which variables",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cause which?\" → output is a graph (DAG, CPDAG, or PAG).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "da-12 (inference): \"Given this DAG, what is the effect of X on Y?\" → DiD,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "RDD, IV, propensity scores, synthetic control, backdoor/frontdoor adjustment.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "If the user already has/assumes a DAG and wants an effect estimate, defer to",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "da-12-ab-testing-causal-inference. Use this skill only when the structure",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The hard truth of discovery: from purely observational data you usually cannot",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "recover a single DAG - only an equivalence class of DAGs (a CPDAG or PAG).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pinning down direction requires extra assumptions (non-Gaussianity, nonlinearity),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "interventions, or time order. Always communicate which edges are oriented vs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. Markov equivalence, CPDAGs, and what is identifiable",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Two DAGs are Markov equivalent if they entail the same conditional",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "independences - they have the same skeleton (undirected edges) and the same",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "v-structures / colliders (A → C ← B with A, B not adjacent). Equivalent DAGs",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cannot be distinguished by observational independence tests alone (Verma & Pearl,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "1990; Andersson, Madigan & Perlman, 1997).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A CPDAG (Completed Partially Directed Acyclic Graph, a.k.a. essential",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "graph) represents the whole Markov equivalence class: directed edges are",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "oriented in every member, undirected edges flip across members.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Constraint- and score-based methods return a CPDAG, not a DAG. Reporting a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "single oriented DAG from such output is a common, serious error.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#1-markov-equivalence-cpdags-and-what-is-identifiable",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Foundational assumptions (state them, always)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Causal Markov condition: each variable is independent of its",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "non-descendants given its parents.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Faithfulness: every conditional independence in the distribution is",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "implied by the graph structure (no exact cancellations). Near-violations cause",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "unstable orientation in finite samples (Spirtes, Glymour & Scheines, 2000).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Causal sufficiency: no unmeasured common causes (latent confounders). PC",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and GES assume this; FCI does not.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Acyclicity: most methods assume a DAG (no feedback loops).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Identifiability hinges on these. Be explicit which the chosen method needs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#2-foundational-assumptions-state-them-always",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "A. Constraint-based (independence-test driven)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "PC algorithm (Peter–Clark; Spirtes, Glymour & Scheines, 2000): start from a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "complete undirected graph, remove edges via conditional-independence (CI) tests,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "then orient colliders and propagate (Meek rules). Output: CPDAG. Assumes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "causal sufficiency + faithfulness. Order-dependence fixed by PC-stable",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(Colombo & Maathuis, 2014). CI tests: Fisher-Z (linear-Gaussian), G²/χ²",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(discrete), KCI (kernel, nonlinear).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "FCI (Fast Causal Inference) and RFCI: drop causal sufficiency - handle",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "latent confounders and selection bias. Output: a PAG (Partial Ancestral",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Graph) over a MAG, with edge marks ○ (unknown), → (ancestor), ↔ (latent",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "common cause) (Spirtes et al., 2000; Zhang, 2008).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#a-constraint-based-independence-test-driven",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "B. Score-based search",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "GES (Greedy Equivalence Search; Chickering, 2002): searches over CPDAG space",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "with a two-phase forward (edge-add) / backward (edge-delete) greedy search,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "scoring with a decomposable, consistent score - BIC (continuous) or",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "BDeu (discrete). Asymptotically returns the true equivalence class. fGES",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "is the fast/parallel variant (TETRAD).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "GIES (Hauser & Bühlmann, 2012): GES extended to interventional data —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "searches over interventional Markov equivalence classes, exploiting experiments",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "to orient more edges.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#b-score-based-search",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "C. Permutation / ordering search",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "GRaSP and BOSS (Lam, Andrews & Ramsey, 2022): search over variable",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#c-permutation-ordering-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "orderings; more accurate and scalable than GES on many benchmarks, available",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#c-permutation-ordering-search",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "in causal-learn and TETRAD.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#c-permutation-ordering-search",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "D. Functional causal models (FCMs) — orient beyond the equivalence class",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "By assuming a functional form, these identify a unique DAG, not just a CPDAG.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "LiNGAM - Linear, Non-Gaussian, Acyclic Model (Shimizu, Hoyer, Hyvärinen &",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Kerminen, 2006, JMLR 7:2003–2030): linear SEM with non-Gaussian noise → full",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "causal order is identifiable. ICA-LiNGAM uses ICA; DirectLiNGAM",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(Shimizu et al., 2011) is regression-based and avoids ICA local optima.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ANM - Additive Noise Models (Hoyer, Janzing, Mooij, Peters & Schölkopf,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "2008/2009): Y = f(X) + N with N ⟂ X. Nonlinear f breaks the X↔Y symmetry →",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cause/effect direction identifiable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Post-Nonlinear (PNL) model (Zhang & Hyvärinen, 2009): Y = g(f(X) + N) - most",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "general identifiable FCM. In causal-learn.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#d-functional-causal-models-fcms-orient-beyond-the-equivalence-class",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "E. Continuous-optimization / gradient methods",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reframe combinatorial DAG search as smooth optimization with a differentiable",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "acyclicity constraint - scales and integrates with deep learning.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "NOTEARS (Zheng, Aragam, Ravikumar & Xing, NeurIPS 2018): the acyclicity",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "breakthrough - h(W) = tr(e^{W∘W}) − d = 0 is a smooth, exact characterization",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "of acyclicity, solved via augmented Lagrangian. Originally linear; NOTEARS-MLP",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "extends to nonlinear.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "GOLEM (Ng, Ghassami & Zhang, NeurIPS 2020): likelihood-based score with soft",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "acyclicity - faster and more accurate than NOTEARS in the linear-Gaussian/EV",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DAG-GNN (Yu et al., ICML 2019): VAE/GNN variant for nonlinear and discrete",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Caveat: Reisach, Seiler & Weichwein (NeurIPS 2021, \"Beware of the Simulated",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DAG\") showed continuous-optimization methods can exploit varsortability —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "marginal-variance artifacts of synthetic data scaling. Standardize data and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "don't trust synthetic-benchmark wins blindly.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#e-continuous-optimization-gradient-methods",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "F. Time-series causal discovery",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Granger causality: X Granger-causes Y if past X improves prediction of Y",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "beyond Y's own past. Predictive, not structural; fails with latent confounders /",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "instantaneous effects / nonlinearity. Use only as a baseline.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PCMCI / PCMCI+ (Runge et al., Science Advances 2019; PCMCI+ in UAI 2020):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "two-stage - a PC-style condition-selection step, then **Momentary Conditional",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Independence (MCI)** tests controlling for autocorrelation and indirect links.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PCMCI+ adds contemporaneous links. Implemented in Tigramite; pairs with any",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "CI test (ParCorr, GPDC, CMI). LPCMCI handles latent confounders.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "VAR-LiNGAM (Hyvärinen et al., 2010): combines a VAR model with LiNGAM to",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "recover both lagged and instantaneous causal effects.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#f-time-series-causal-discovery",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tools / Frameworks",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "causal-learn (py-why, Python; Zheng et al., 2024; docs",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "https://causal-learn.readthedocs.io/): the reference Python toolkit - PC, FCI,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "GES, GRaSP, BOSS, LiNGAM family, ANM, PNL, CD-NOD, plus CI tests and graph",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "utilities. Default first choice for general discovery.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "gCastle (Huawei Noah's Ark Lab; Zhang et al., 2021): gradient-based focus",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(NOTEARS, GOLEM, DAG-GNN, GraN-DAG, ...), PyTorch + GPU, data simulators, and a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "built-in metrics module (SHD, FDR, TPR, F1, NNZ).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Tigramite (Runge; https://github.com/jakobrunge/tigramite): the standard for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "time-series discovery (PCMCI, PCMCI+, LPCMCI, RPCMCI).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pcalg (R; Kalisch et al., JSS 2012): mature PC/FCI/RFCI/GES with IDA effect",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DoWhy (py-why; https://www.pywhy.org/dowhy/): primarily inference, but its",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "GCM module and dowhy.causal_discovery wrap discovery; good for the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "discover-then-refute workflow.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "CausalNex (QuantumBlack): NOTEARS-based structure learning + Bayesian-network",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "reasoning, with expert-knowledge constraints (tabu edges, required edges).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "TETRAD / py-tetrad: large library of search algorithms and the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "knowledge/background-constraint framework.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Practical Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Always inject background knowledge. Forbidden edges, required edges, and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "tiered time order (a cause can't follow its effect) dramatically reduce the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "equivalence class. Every major tool supports knowledge/tabu constraints - use",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Match method to assumptions and data type:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Possible latent confounders → FCI / RFCI (get a PAG), not PC/GES.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Linear + non-Gaussian noise → DirectLiNGAM (gets a full DAG).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonlinear, continuous → ANM / PNL, or NOTEARS-MLP / DAG-GNN.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Discrete/categorical → score-based with BDeu, or G²-test PC.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "High-dim time series → PCMCI+.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Have interventions/experiments → GIES or interventional NOTEARS.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Standardize/scale continuous variables before continuous-optimization",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "methods to avoid varsortability artifacts.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Bootstrap for edge stability. Resample, re-run discovery, and report",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "edge-presence and orientation frequencies rather than one point graph.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Discover → refute → estimate. Use discovery to propose a graph, validate",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "with domain experts and refutation/sensitivity checks, then hand the validated",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DAG to da-12 for effect estimation. Discovery output is a hypothesis, not",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Evaluate with the right metric:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "SHD (Structural Hamming Distance): count of edge insert/delete/reverse",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ops to match the truth - lower is better; compare against the CPDAG, not a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DAG, when methods return equivalence classes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "SID (Structural Intervention Distance; Peters & Bühlmann, 2015): counts",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "intervention-distribution errors - closer to what matters for downstream",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "effect estimation than SHD.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Also F1 / precision / recall on the skeleton, FDR, TPR.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reporting a single DAG when the method returns a CPDAG/PAG. Undirected /",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "circle-marked edges are genuinely undetermined; orienting them implies",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "assumptions you didn't make.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Treating Granger causality as structural causality. It's lagged prediction;",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "silent on confounders and contemporaneous effects.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Trusting synthetic-benchmark performance of NOTEARS-family methods without",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "standardizing data (varsortability - Reisach et al., 2021).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Ignoring latent confounders. Running PC/GES when unmeasured common causes are",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "plausible yields confident but wrong edges. Use FCI or sensitivity analysis.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Skipping faithfulness/sufficiency disclosure. Stakeholders must know the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "result is conditional on assumptions that can't be verified from data alone.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Using discovery output directly for policy. Discovery proposes; it does not",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "prove. Validate before acting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Doing effect estimation here. Backdoor adjustment, IV, DiD, propensity",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "scores, synthetic control → da-12-ab-testing-causal-inference.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Troubleshooting",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Too many undirected edges in the CPDAG: expected with observational-only",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "data. Add background knowledge, use an FCM method (LiNGAM/ANM) if assumptions",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "hold, or collect interventional data.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Unstable edges across runs/bootstraps: likely faithfulness near-violations,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "small n, or wrong CI test. Increase data, switch CI test (e.g., KCI for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "nonlinearity), use PC-stable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PC gives different graphs depending on variable order: use PC-stable",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(Colombo & Maathuis, 2014).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Dense, implausible graph from NOTEARS: increase the L1 sparsity penalty,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "standardize data, threshold small weights; consider GOLEM.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonlinear relationships missed: linear methods (Fisher-Z PC, linear NOTEARS,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "LiNGAM) can't see them - use KCI tests, ANM/PNL, NOTEARS-MLP, or DAG-GNN.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Time-series links look confounded by autocorrelation: that's exactly what",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PCMCI (MCI step) controls for; plain Granger does not.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-32-causal-discovery/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
